THIS LICENSE DOES NOT COVER THE WHOLE TREE.

Two directories carry their own terms and are not MIT:

  patches/linux/        GPL-2.0-only.  These are patches against the Linux
                        kernel.  A patch is a derivative work of the file it
                        modifies, so it inherits the kernel's license; this
                        is not a choice the repository makes.  See
                        patches/linux/README.md.

  bootloader/vendor/    Apache-2.0, and a further 63 files Apache-2.0 OR MIT.
                        Vendored unmodified from ESP-IDF, with the per-file
                        SPDX headers intact and the provenance recorded in
                        bootloader/vendor/MANIFEST.md.  Redistributed under
                        Espressif's terms, not relicensed.

Everything else -- bootloader/p4/, board/ (including board/hget/), dts/,
tools/, config/ and docs/ -- is original work under the MIT license above.

Note that a built bootloader binary links the vendored Apache-2.0 sources,
so the binary must carry Apache-2.0 attribution even though the sources
written here are MIT.  The two licenses are compatible; this is an
attribution obligation, not a conflict.
